Her extreme uneasiness turned into fear, and then the fear caused the tears to start falling from her eyes. Meanwhile, Matthias’s deep-blue eyes remained fixed on her, revealing nothing of his inner feelings.
“And so… I’ll do as you say. I’ll move to the capital with Uncle Bill. I was embarrassed to think of living that way before, so I wanted to escape, but I don’t think I could anymore.” She looked intently at him.

He slowly stood up and walked towards her. “So just like that, you’re okay with being my mistress?” he asked in a voice so cold as to sound heartless.
She lowered her head in embarrassment, but it was no use. He lifted her chin and made her look at him again. She felt overwhelmed by his searching gaze as he stared at her.
Feeling unable to speak, she simply nodded her head. She could feel her heart pounding in her chest, and she hoped he couldn’t hear it. Please, Layla, she thought to herself, please succeed in footing him with this lie!
Gripping his arm with her trembling hand, she said, “I’ll d-do it on one condition "
“A condition?”
“Yes. I don’t accept deals that I get nothing out of. I learned that from someone.”
The doubtful look on his face softened considerably at this remark, which gave her the courage to go on.
“Are you going to accept my condition?” she asked. “Tell me what it is.”
“I want you to promise first.”
“You want me to promise to accept a condition on a deal without knowing what the condition is?” he asked, frowning. “Why should I? Who are you to demand that of me?”
“I’m Layla,” she replied, not backing down. “I’m your Layla.”
He chuckled at her bold reply. All she could do now was pray internally that her ploy would succeed.
For a moment, he looked out the window and saw the starry night sky reflected in the river. His gaze then slowly shifted back inside, passing over the

paintings covering the wall, and came to a stop on her face, which he stared at deeply. “Tell me the condition, Layla.”
“Does that mean you promise to accept it?” She pleadingly tightened her grip on his arm, like a child pestering her parent.
He chuckled once again. “Sure.” He let go of her chin and cupped her cheek. As he gazed into her joyful, light-green eyes, his smile grew much warmer. “I promise.”







“You’re sending Bill Remmer to the Ratse mansion?” Dowager Herhardt asked, looking at her grandson with surprise.
Her daughter-in-law, Elise von Herhardt, who had been calmly enjoying the music they were listening to, soon put on a shocked expression as well.
Matthias alone remained calm, despite having caused the stir himself. “Yes, that’s the plan.”
“That’s a very sudden and unexpected thing to do, Matthias.”
“Mother has been displeased with Mr. Remmer ever since the accident. And besides, Mr. Remmer is getting to be too old to handle being in charge of Arvis’s large garden.”
“That’s true, but…” As Elise trailed off, she looked to her mother-in-law for support.
However, Dowager Herhardt couldn’t dispute the points Matthias had made either.

While his mother and grandmother were reduced to silence, Matthias took a sip of coffee. Now that Layla had made up her mind, there was no need for further delay. There was no particular need to hide his relationship with her, either.
The condition she had requested was not what he had expected at all: I want us to be lovers” With a very sad expression on her face, she had gone on. “Once you’re married, I’ll have to leave Arvis. I’ll never be able to return here.”
