Do You Really Think I’m Pretty?






Winter break came to an end, and Layla was reunited with her students. Many	of	them	had	grown	noticeably	during	the	interim.
Unfortunately, their unruliness had also grown, which made for a hectic first day back.
“Miss Llewellyn! I finished all the problems!” a boy shouted, holding his slate up in the air.
Startled out of her momentary reverie, Layla walked over and took the slate from him. “Wow, you’re done already? You must have practiced your arithmetic during the break!”
The young boy beamed at her praise and started blushing.
As soon as she had graded the boy’s quiz and handed it back to him, Monica burst into tears. The boy sitting behind her had started pulling on her ponytail. Layla consoled Monica, scolded the boy, and resumed class.

The long first day of school progressed in this manner before finally coming to an end.
After seeing off the students, she returned to the classroom, which looked like a warzone. Sitting at her desk, she looked out the window and saw yellowish-green leaves just starting to sprout from the tree branches. At this point, one still had to look closely to seethe signs of the change of seasons, but it wouldn’t be long before the whole landscape would! be transformed into spring. Before that happened, she had to finish her plan.
She picked up her bag to leave. The mere thought of being lovers with someone as demonic as the duke made her shudder, but since she knew that the sweeter the lie she told was, the deeper the pain he would feel, she was able to endure ft.
She had been so delighted after the first night she deceived him, she had barely been able to get to sleep. It was the first happiness he had ever given her. Before exiting the classroom, she let down her hair and put on some light makeup. Despite all her practice, she couldn’t get the makeup to look like she wanted it to, which disappointed her. She thought about wiping it off, but
there wasn’t much time left before her date.
She felt dirty dolling herself up for that horrible man. To rid herself of the feeling, she forced a smile, telling herself, Make the prettiest smile you can because your smile wits turn into the poison that you’ll use to bring him down.







Matthias brought his car to a stop near the corner by the village school. It was his first time driving in quite a while, but he hadn’t forgotten how. Of course, when he had told them he was going out driving on his own, his assistant and his chauffeur had reacted like they were witnessing the end of the world
He checked his watch, then looked out the car window at the school. Just in time, Layla came walking out of the school. Her golden hair fluttered with each step as she strode down the sidewalk.
He calmly watched the quiet, busily moving woman. Ever since he had first seen her all those years earlier, she had always reminded him of a small bird nimbly flying through the air.
Apparently she hadn’t expected that he would be waiting for her because even as she passed right in front of the car, she didn’t slow down her walking pace at all. He tapped on the car window to summon his busy bird.
She flinched and came to a stop. Confusion soon spread across her face.
Chuckling, he opened the door and got out of the car. She reflexively took a step back, then looked at him with her head slightly cocked. “Your Grace… what are you doing here? This isn’t where we were supposed to meet.”
“Why do you think I might be here?”
“Did you come here to pick me up?” She peered inside the car. “Did you drive here yourself?she asked, looking as shocked as his chauffeur had looked earlier.

He walked around the front of the car and opened the passenger door.
Holding the strap of her bag tightly, she hesitantly walked towards him.
Once she was closer, he noticed that her face looked a little different from normal. “Are you wearing makeup?” he asked, sounding amused.
It was an innocent question, but she reacted like a child who had been caught being naughty. “Does it look weird?” she asked.
